<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Composer Evaluator’s training setup per dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During small-scale search, the HNAS Evaluator evaluates each candidate hybrid LLM architecture provided by the HNAS Engine.
We provide details on the training and validation setup the HNAS evaluator uses.
This setup changes depending on the dataset used for evaluation.
Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ D.1 Search Training/Validation Setup ‣ Appendix D Experimental Details ‣ Composer: A Search Framework for Hybrid Neural Architecture Design" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> details the training setup for each dataset.
We explore three datasets: MAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Poli et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Sampled-DCLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and BabiStories <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
For MAD and BabiStories, we follow the same training setup <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Poli et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
For Sampled-DCLM, we reduce the sample size 12K samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Model Size and FLOPs Calculation</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We describe size (number of parameters) and FLOPs calculations per computational primitive: Grouped Query Attention (GQA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ainslie et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and SwiGLU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shazeer, 2020</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention:</span>
We provide a general formulation for calculating FLOPs (forward and backward pass) and parameter size of a single Attention layer that can be applied to both GQA or MHA layers.
We follow DeepMind’s calculations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoffmann et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, calculating FLOPs for the forward and backward pass.</p>
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attn Parameter Count}=2\times\text{$dim$}^{2}+2\times\frac{\text{$dim$}}{\text{$num\_heads$}}\times\text{$num\_kv\_heads$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Attn Parameter Count</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attn Parameter Count}=2\times\text{$dim$}^{2}+2\times\frac{\text{$dim$}}{\text{$num\_heads$}}\times\text{$num\_kv\_heads$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\text{Attn FLOPs}=&amp;\ 6\times\text{$dim$}^{2}+6\times 2\times\frac{\text{$dim$}}{\text{$num\_heads$}}\times\text{$num\_kv\_heads$}\\
&amp;+6\times\text{$dim$}^{2}+3\times 2\times 2\times\text{$num\_heads$}\times\text{$dim$}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mtext>Attn FLOPs</mtext><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn> 6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\text{Attn FLOPs}=&amp;\ 6\times\text{$dim$}^{2}+6\times 2\times\frac{\text{$dim$}}{\text{$num\_heads$}}\times\text{$num\_kv\_heads$}\\
&amp;+6\times\text{$dim$}^{2}+3\times 2\times 2\times\text{$num\_heads$}\times\text{$dim$}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MLP (SwiGLU):</span></p>
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{MLP Parameter Count}=3\times\text{$dim$}\times\text{$hidden\_dim$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>MLP Parameter Count</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{MLP Parameter Count}=3\times\text{$dim$}\times\text{$hidden\_dim$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{MLP FLOPs}=6\times 3\times\text{$dim$}\times\text{$hidden\_dim$}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>MLP FLOPs</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{MLP FLOPs}=6\times 3\times\text{$dim$}\times\text{$hidden\_dim$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
